        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The grey seal, <i>Halichoerus</i> <i>grypus</i>, is an aquatic mammal that lives in the North Atlantic Ocean. It feeds on fish, which it hunts at depths of up to 70 metres.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 10.1 shows a grey seal.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig10.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 10.1",
            "src": "figures/q10_fig10_1.png",
            "alt": "Seal",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Diving to hunt for fish has an effect on the respiration of the grey seal.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A study was carried out to measure the blood lactate concentration of a grey seal before, during and after a dive in deep water.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 22
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 10.2 shows the results of this study.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 23
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig10.2",
            "caption": "Fig. 10.2",
            "src": "figures/q10_fig10_2.png",
            "alt": "Blood lactate concentration during and after a dive",
            "source": {
              "qp": 23
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With reference to Fig. 10.2, suggest reasons for the change in blood lactate concentration of the seal:",
            "source": {
              "qp": 23
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "items": [
              "during the dive",
              "after the dive."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "marks": 4,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "12.2(10)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 4,
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>four</i></b><i> from: </i>  <i>during – increase in lactate concentration </i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "1  (initially) lactate <u>concentration</u> low due to aerobic respiration <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "2  no / less, oxygen available so (increase in) anaerobic respiration <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "3  pyruvate, reduced / converted, to lactate <b>; </b>  <i>after</i> – <i>decrease in lactate concentration </i>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "4  (more) oxygen available so aerobic respiration occurs <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "text": "5  lactate, oxidised / converted, to pyruvate <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 6,
              "text": "6  idea that lactate is processed by liver <b>; </b> <b> </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 7,
              "text": "7  AVP <b>; </b>e.g. <i>ref. to</i> oxygen debt / EPOC<i> </i>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Fermentation regenerates NAD so that glycolysis can continue. After exercise, extra oxygen supports recovery processes, including the metabolism of accumulated lactate.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:12.2(10)",
                "ms:a#1"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Connect limited oxygen availability to continued glycolysis.",
            "Link recovery oxygen uptake to removal or conversion of lactate."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
            {
              "text": "Saying that lactate is produced by aerobic respiration",
              "basis": "inferred",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:12.2(10)"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "type": "short"
      },
      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 24,
